# reel's code demo: reel walks through a little of its own source, in Swift and then in Java, narrated by the same
# voice as its other demos. `mise run demos code` records it. A code screen is reel's own editor, drawn a frame at a
# time: nothing to install, no window, no permissions. The files are copies in demos/code, so the lines stay put.
Import //demos/reel.reelpreset
Screen code

Output //docs/media/code.mp4
Output //docs/media/code.gif
Set Viewport 1100x620
Set FontSize 20
# reel's own stings open and close it, as they do the other demos; the square cut gets title cards.
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,600ms square ? "reel" "Code too" : 2s
Outro@fade,800ms square ? "Recorded with reel" "brew install --cask mpdreamz/tap/reel" : 2s

Code code/SpeechClock.swift
Say "Reel walks through code too, in an editor of its own. Nothing to install, and no permissions."
Go "public mutating func say"
Focus lines 9-20
Say "This is how reel keeps one narrated line from talking over the next."
Mark "max(now, speechEnd)" 1
Callout "max(now, speechEnd)" "when it's reached, or after the line before"
Say "A line starts when the reel reaches it, or when the one before it ends."
Callout off
Mark "speechEnd = start + line.duration" 2
Say "And it ends a line's length later."
Mark off
Focus off
Code code/SpeechClock.java at "public double[] say"
Say "The same in Java. Dozens of languages, coloured as your editor colours them."
Go "return new double[]"
Key end
Key return
Zoom cursor 1.5x
Type@60ms "// typed at your pace, as you would"
Sleep 600ms
Zoom off
Say "And that's a take."
Sleep 1s
